<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 14.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - May 14.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Feng Kang	 48,000   May 5     May 18     Inchon</p>
<p> Jade Orient     30,000   May 18    May 25     Inchon</p>
<p> Grande	    45,000   May 31    Jun  8     Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   Jun 20		   Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta Trident   35,000   Jun 6		    Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Jade Pacific    28,000   May 3     May 14     KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Pac Duck	  30,000   May 10    May 27     POSCO</p>
<p> Thornhill	 35,512   May 19		   Kangwon</p>
<p> Nurten Ana	33,000   May 25		   Kangwon</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Western Friend  36,500   May 11    May 24     POSCO</p>
<p> Aspidoforos     30,500   May 20		   POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yan	  50,000   Jun End		  POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian Trident 35,000   Jun End		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Pisces Pioneer  28,361   May 14		   Hanbo</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5650</p>
